{title: This Blood}
{key: G}
{x_theme: healing, praise, blood, cross, easter}
{x_source: chrd:this_blood.chrd}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]There is a blood that [C/G]cost a  [G]life
That paid my [D]way, death its [G]price
When it flowed down from the [C]cross
My sins were [G]gone, my sins for[D]got
There is a [G]grave that [C]tried to [G]hide
This precious [D]blood that gave me [G]life
In Three Days He breathed a[C]gain
And rose to [G]stand in my de[D]fense

{comment: Verse 2}
There is a [G]Blood that [C]sights the [G]blind
That Heals the [D]sick the lonely [G]finds
It has the Power to [G/B]free the [C]bound
As chains they [G]fall upon the [D]ground
So pour it [G]out and to [C]cleanse my [G]soul
And let His [D]liquid Glory [G]flow
Because it lives to [G/B]make me [C]whole
I owe my [G]life, I owe my [D]all

{comment: Verse 3}
There is a [G]grave that [C]tried to [G]hide
This precious [D]blood that gave me [G]life
But in Three Days He [G/B]breathed [C]again
And rose to [G/B]stand   [G]in my de[D7]fense

{comment: Chorus}
So I [G]come to tell you He's alive
To tell you [D/Gb]that He  [Em]dries [D]every tear that [C]falls
So I [G]come to tell you that He saves
To shout and [D/Gb]to    pro[Em]claim that He's [D]coming back for [C]you

{comment: Interlude}
This [G]life, this [D]price, this [Em]blood, this [C]one
This [G]life He [D]paid the [Em]price with precious [C]blood

{comment: Bridge}
[G]What can wash away my sin?
[Em]Nothing, [C]nothing!
[G]What can make me whole again?
[Em]Nothing but the blood, [C]nothing but the blood!
[G]What can wash away my sin?
[Em]Nothing, [C]nothing!
[G]What can make me whole again?
[Em]Nothing but the blood, [C]nothing but the blood!
